          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong dynamical system
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (often a bare
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            or a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A \times X \longrightarrow X
                  \\,.
          %p
            To model continuous
            = succeed "-evolution" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time"} time
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = (\mathbb{R}, +)
            to be the additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %p
            For discrete time evolution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = (\mathbb{Z}, +)
            is the additive group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            (or just the monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{N}, +)
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+value+problem"} initial value problem
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+equation"} differential equation
            “of evolution type”.
          %p
            In this case, the dynamical system is equivalently a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            (this being the action of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+element"} unit element
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p Sometimes the evolution is only partially defined; this is most often in dynamical systems induced by evolution differential equations which do not necessarily have existence of solutions for arbitrary large time, or the dynamical system is defined only for nonnegative time.
          %p
            The definition evidently makes sense quite generally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
            various ambient
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+dynamics"} algebraic dynamics
          %p Dynamical systems are used to describe not only physical motions but also the behaviour of parameters of various systems, e.g. in sociological, financial, weather and other models.
          %h2#literature Literature
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+systems+theory"} categorical systems theory
            %li
